    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36962" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pōmētĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f. (collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pōmē tii</span></b> ,
		ōrum, m., <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 6,
		775</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a very
				old town of the Volsci</i>, <i>in Latium</i>, <i>also called</i> Suessa Pometia; perh. the mod. <i>Torre Petrara</i> or <i>Mesa</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Rep. 2, 24, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 53</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 25
			al.</span></i>—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pōmētīnus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Pometia</i>, <i>Pometian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manubiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
					55</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
